  "answer": "To reduce the risk that a government-led AI arms race causes actors to skimp on alignment and safety, it has been proposed to implement cross-cultural education initiatives (https://longtermrisk.org/international-cooperation-vs-ai-arms-race/). The proposed mechanism involves governments and NGOs creating media campaigns, exchange programs, and educational curricula that emphasize global citizenship (https://longtermrisk.org/international-cooperation-vs-ai-arms-race/). By promoting moral tolerance and multiculturalism, these initiatives aim to shape public attitudes so that people care less about which nation wins, thereby lowering the public and elite appetite for national AI supremacy (https://longtermrisk.org/international-cooperation-vs-ai-arms-race/). Reducing nationalism fosters international cooperation and diminishes the competitive risk-taking pressures in interstate AI competition, lessening the incentives for actors to accept higher technical and ethical risks just to beat their rivals (https://longtermrisk.org/international-cooperation-vs-ai-arms-race/)."
